# context/document-mirrors.brix -- one document, several homes, proven identical.
#
# WHY. A document sometimes belongs in more than one room, and the usual answers are both poor:
# move it and break every inbound reference, or copy it and let the copies drift apart in the dark.
# A third answer is available to a tree that already measures things. DECLARE the homes here, and
# let a witness prove every home holds the same bytes. Divergence becomes a red on the lap it
# enters rather than a discovery months later.
#
# This is Tablecloth's own idea reaching the document shelf: content addressed by its hash, so
# sameness is a fact a machine checks rather than a promise a person keeps.
#
# SHAPE. One `mirror` block per document. `canonical` names the copy that is edited; `at` names
# each additional home, and the witness copies canonical over every `at` when asked to `write`.
# Edit the canonical, run the write, commit both -- never edit a mirror by hand.
#
#   mirror <name>
#   canonical <path>
#   at <path>
#
# Proven by tools/d/document_mirror_witness.rish over tools/fixtures/document_mirror_scan.sh.
# Seated 20260823.173634 on Keaton's word.

mirror kyri-voice
canonical context/KYRI.md
at ember-voices/KYRI.md

mirror spellbook
canonical context/SPELLBOOK.md
at spellbook/README.md

mirror chemical-formulas
canonical context/CHEMICAL_FORMULAS.md
at biochemistry/README.md

# A NAMING NOTE, and a fault this descriptor was built with. Keaton offered two homes for the
# voices: `ember/voices/` and `ember-voices/`. The first was tried and is wrong for a reason that
# has nothing to do with taste: **a mirror is byte-identical, and a relative link is depth-dependent**,
# so `../foundations/x.md` resolves from `context/` (depth 1) and lands on `ember/foundations/x.md`
# from `ember/voices/` (depth 2). Eight links broke the moment the canonical gained them. `ember-voices/`
# stands at depth 1 beside `context/`, so every relative link resolves identically from both homes.
#
# The rule that follows, and the guard now proves it: **every home of a mirrored document must sit at
# the same depth**, or the copies cannot be byte-identical and correct at once. Recorded as REDS %176.
#
# It also settles a second thing the elder note raised. `ember/voices/` read as a room named after one
# of its own contents, since **Ember is one of the four voices Kyri carries**. At the root the name is
# a compound rather than a containment, and the inversion goes away.
